[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
# Purpose and workflow

Implementation records define work, verification strategy, repeatable test
procedures, and completed evidence.

Use immutable UIDs with this form:

```text
IMP-[MODULE]-[TYPE]-[NNN]
```

Supported type segments are:

- `TASK` for implementation tasks
- `PLAN` for test plans
- `TEST` for test cases
- `VER` for verification and validation records.

Planning artifacts describe intended work. Verification records describe
completed checks. Completing a task does not verify a requirement.

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    REQ[Requirement] --> DES[Design]
    DES --> TASK[Task]
    TASK --> PLAN[Test plan]
    PLAN --> TEST[Test case]
    TEST --> VER[Verification record]
```

A `Child` relation represents a dependency. The referenced record must be
satisfied before the dependent activity begins, unless an approved exception is
recorded.
<<<

