[IMPLEMENTATION]
UID: IMP-TEMPLATE-TEST-001
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: Template nominal functional test
PHASE: Verification
TYPE: TestCase
SAFETY_RELEVANCE: NotSafetyRelated
INDEPENDENCE: Peer
STATEMENT: Verify that the template component produces the specified functional result under nominal conditions.
PREREQUISITES: Approved test plan, completed implementation task, controlled environment, and identified test data.
OUTPUTS: Test report, raw logs, actual result, expected-result comparison, and anomaly references.
TEST_LEVEL: Component
TEST_METHOD: Automated
PROCEDURE: >>>
1. Configure the identified component baseline.
2. Establish the specified nominal preconditions.
3. Provide the defined valid input.
4. Observe the externally visible output and state.
5. Retain raw logs and configuration identification.
<<<
EXPECTED_RESULT: The component produces the measurable result required by REQ-TEMPLATE-FR-001 without a prohibited side effect.
RESULT: Pending
RATIONALE: The case independently checks the nominal functional behavior.
TAGS: template, test-case, functional
