- TYPE: Child
  VALUE: IMP-TEMPLATE-TASK-001
  ROLE: Depends on

[IMPLEMENTATION]
UID: IMP-TEMPLATE-TEST-002
STATUS: Planned
TITLE: Template safety-boundary and fault-response test
PHASE: Verification
TYPE: TestCase
SAFETY_RELEVANCE: SafetyCritical
INDEPENDENCE: IndependentPerson
STATEMENT: Verify that invalid, missing, stale, duplicated, reordered, malformed, unauthorized, or excessive-rate input cannot prevent the required protective-stop response.
PREREQUISITES: Approved test plan, integrated candidate baseline, controlled fault-injection capability, calibrated equipment, and approved acceptance criteria.
OUTPUTS: Raw fault-injection data, timing results, logs, configuration records, report, and anomaly references.
TEST_LEVEL: Integration
TEST_METHOD: FaultInjection
PROCEDURE: >>>
1. Identify hardware, software, parameters, calibration, and interface revision.
2. Establish each approved initial state and operating mode.
3. Inject each specified interface or dependency fault separately.
4. Demand the protective-stop safety function.
5. Measure detection, logic, communication, actuation, and safe-state timing.
6. Confirm diagnostics, latching, reset, and restart behavior.
7. Repeat justified fault combinations and environmental boundary conditions.
8. Retain raw evidence and all deviations from the approved procedure.
<<<
EXPECTED_RESULT: The system rejects or contains invalid input, reaches the validated safe state within the allocated response time, reports required diagnostics, and inhibits restart until reset conditions are satisfied.
RESULT: Pending
RATIONALE: The test directly evaluates the boundary assumptions and fault behavior relied upon by the safety architecture.
TAGS: template, test-case, safety, fault-injection
