[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
# Execution rules

Safety-related evidence is valid only for an identified configuration. Record,
as applicable:

- product variant and specimen identity
- hardware revision
- software and firmware commit or immutable build
- parameter and calibration versions
- model, map, and test-data versions
- interface and procedure revisions
- tool and test-equipment versions
- calibration status
- environmental, surface, and loading conditions
- deviations from the approved procedure.

Evidence must be durable, access controlled, reviewable, and retained under the
project policy. A mutable dashboard must not be the only evidence.

Do not edit a failed record into a passing record. Create a new execution
record and preserve the failed result and disposition.

Implementation is complete only when outputs exist, required reviews and checks
are complete, verification evidence is tied to the tested baseline, failures
have dispositions, traceability is complete, required independence is
satisfied, and unresolved anomalies are accepted by authorized roles.
<<<
